{"parentUuid":"044e500d-578d-4c18-b049-c215aa2e9e32","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6e1f01cb-4356-4ba8-94e6-90a7c6c916fa","agentId":"a7f6f2df056acf347","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NeNaCqpYmMzKL11v8oeiFP","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Claude Sonnet 4.6 SWE-bench HumanEval benchmark 2026 code generation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Claude Sonnet 4.6: 79.6% SWE-bench at $3/MTok — Complete Guide (2026) | NxCode\",\"url\":\"https://www.nxcode.io/resources/news/claude-sonnet-4-6-complete-guide-benchmarks-pricing-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Claude Sonnet 4.6 Review. Anthropic released Claude Sonnet 4.6 on… | by Barnacle Goose | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@leucopsis/claude-sonnet-4-6-review-e01cc9d31273\"},{\"title\":\"Claude Sonnet 4.6: Features, Access, Tests, and Benchmarks | DataCamp\",\"url\":\"https://www.datacamp.com/blog/claude-sonnet-4-6\"},{\"title\":\"Claude Benchmarks (2026): Every Score for Opus 4.6, Sonnet 4.6 & Haiku\",\"url\":\"https://www.morphllm.com/claude-benchmarks\"},{\"title\":\"AI Coding Benchmarks 2026 — SWE-bench, HumanEval & Model Rankings | Singularity Moments\",\"url\":\"https://www.singularitymoments.com/ai-coding-benchmark-swe-bench/\"},{\"title\":\"Best AI Coding Models 2026: SWE-Bench Leaderboard (Claude, GPT-5, Gemini) | Local AI Master\",\"url\":\"https://localaimaster.com/models/best-ai-coding-models\"},{\"title\":\"Best LLMs for Coding in 2026: SWE-bench, HumanEval, and LiveCode Rankings | Onyx AI\",\"url\":\"https://onyx.app/insights/best-llms-for-coding-2026\"},{\"title\":\"SWE-Bench Pro Leaderboard AI Coding Benchmark (Public Dataset) | Scale\",\"url\":\"https://labs.scale.com/leaderboard/swe_bench_pro_public\"},{\"title\":\"Claude Sonnet 4.6 in Production: Capability, Safety, and Cost Explained | Caylent\",\"url\":\"https://caylent.com/blog/claude-sonnet-4-6-in-production-capability-safety-and-cost-explained\"},{\"title\":\"SWE-Bench Verified Benchmark Leaderboard\",\"url\":\"https://llm-stats.com/benchmarks/swe-bench-verified\"}]\n\nI've successfully performed the web search. Here's a summary of the findings about Claude Sonnet 4.6 and its performance on SWE-bench and HumanEval benchmarks:\n\n## Claude Sonnet 4.6 Benchmark Performance\n\nClaude Sonnet 4.6 was released on February 17, 2026, achieving 79.6% on SWE-bench Verified and 72.5% on OSWorld.\n\n### Key Code Generation Benchmarks:\n\n**SWE-bench Verified:** Sonnet 4.6 achieves 79.6% SWE-bench Verified, within 1-2 points of Opus 4.6. This score surpasses Sonnet 4.5 by 2.4 points.\n\n**HumanEval:** Sonnet 4.6 scores 92.1% on HumanEval.\n\n### Other Notable Benchmarks:\n\n- LiveCodeBench: 72.4%\n- Terminal-Bench: 59.1%\n- OSWorld-Verified (72.5%) tests autonomous computer use\n\n### Context and Features:\n\nSonnet 4.6 introduces a 1 million token context window (beta), making it the first Sonnet-class model to support full codebase analysis in a single prompt.\n\n### Overall Capability:\n\nMath performance represents a massive 27-point jump from Sonnet 4.5's 62% to 89%, indicating significant improvements in quantitative reasoning alongside coding capabilities.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4884f05c-313e-4e3e-8510-29bd020a7ea3","timestamp":"2026-05-10T00:10:14.620Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"044e500d-578d-4c18-b049-c215aa2e9e32","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b1105f68-06ff-46fe-bd70-d84297a7d6db","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6e1f01cb-4356-4ba8-94e6-90a7c6c916fa","agentId":"a7f6f2df056acf347","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012JNntU1APYZ7pbc58Unzj3","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"DeepSeek V4 flash pro benchmark code generation 2026 SWE-bench LiveCodeBench\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro · Hugging Face\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro\"},{\"title\":\"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash · Hugging Face\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek V4 (2026): Specs, Benchmarks, API Pricing, and Architecture Guide | Morph\",\"url\":\"https://www.morphllm.com/deepseek-v4\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek V4 Complete Guide (2026): Pro vs Flash, Benchmarks, Pricing, Setup\",\"url\":\"https://codersera.com/blog/deepseek-v4-complete-guide-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek V4-Pro Review: Benchmarks, Pricing & Architecture\",\"url\":\"https://www.buildfastwithai.com/blogs/deepseek-v4-pro-review-2026\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek V4\",\"url\":\"https://www.vals.ai/models/deepseek_deepseek-v4-pro\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek V4 Pro vs Flash: Which One for Production? | WaveSpeed Blog\",\"url\":\"https://wavespeed.ai/blog/posts/deepseek-v4-pro-vs-flash/\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek V4 Review. DeepSeek released V4 as a public… | by Barnacle Goose | Apr, 2026 | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@leucopsis/deepseek-v4-review-a23ce940151c\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek V4 Benchmarks: Full Score Breakdown (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://framia.pro/page/en-US/news/deepseek-v4-benchmarks\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek V4 Flash: Review, Pricing & When to Use It (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://www.buildfastwithai.com/blogs/deepseek-v4-flash-review-2026\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here are the key benchmark results for DeepSeek V4 Flash and Pro models on code generation benchmarks:\n\n## SWE-bench Verified (Software Engineering Benchmark)\n\nV4-Pro-Max scores 80.6% on SWE-bench Verified, and V4-Flash scores 79.0% on SWE-bench Verified. V4-Pro-Max matches Claude Opus 4.6 on SWE-bench (80.6% vs 80.8%).\n\n## LiveCodeBench\n\nV4-Pro-Max scores 93.5 on LiveCodeBench, while V4-Flash scores 91.6% on LiveCodeBench. V4-Pro-Max leads all models on LiveCodeBench (93.5).\n\n## Key Details\n\nDeepSeek-V4-Pro has 1.6T parameters (49B activated) and DeepSeek-V4-Flash has 284B parameters (13B activated) — both supporting a context length of one million tokens. It achieves top-tier performance in coding benchmarks.\n\nThe results show that V4-Pro-Max is particularly strong on code generation tasks, especially on LiveCodeBench where it outperforms all competitors, while maintaining near-parity with leading closed-source models on SWE-bench.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c1d7430e-9146-44e9-ae6e-7ce38bb8a542","timestamp":"2026-05-10T00:10:15.881Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b1105f68-06ff-46fe-bd70-d84297a7d6db","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c5ff5ad0-1ecc-4a31-842c-27eef1fffa66","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6e1f01cb-4356-4ba8-94e6-90a7c6c916fa","agentId":"a7f6f2df056acf347","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DNaYvvdSWTJoBJ9uVpCtg2","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Aider polyglot benchmark leaderboard 2026 Claude Sonnet DeepSeek\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SWE-Bench Verified Leaderboard March 2026 - Marco Patzelt\",\"url\":\"https://www.marc0.dev/en/leaderboard\"},{\"title\":\"I Tested 15 LLMs on 38 Real Coding Tasks. Here's My Routing Table.\",\"url\":\"https://ianlpaterson.com/blog/llm-benchmark-2026-38-actual-tasks-15-models-for-2-29/\"},{\"title\":\"Aider LLM Leaderboards | aider\",\"url\":\"https://aider.chat/docs/leaderboards/\"},{\"title\":\"LLM Coding Benchmark (May 2026): DeepSeek v4, Kimi v2.6, Grok 4.3, GPT 5.5 – AkitaOnRails.com\",\"url\":\"https://akitaonrails.com/en/2026/04/24/llm-benchmarks-parte-3-deepseek-kimi-mimo/\"},{\"title\":\"Aider Benchmark Leaderboard\",\"url\":\"https://llm-stats.com/benchmarks/aider\"},{\"title\":\"LLM Benchmarks 2026: 30+ Models Ranked — MMLU, SWE-bench, Arena Elo & Pricing\",\"url\":\"https://iternal.ai/llm-selection-guide\"},{\"title\":\"AI Coding Benchmarks 2026: Every Major Eval Explained and Ranked\",\"url\":\"https://www.morphllm.com/ai-coding-benchmarks-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Best LLM for Coding in 2026 (Benchmarks + Real Tests)\",\"url\":\"https://www.crackr.dev/blog/best-llm-for-coding\"},{\"title\":\"SWE-bench Leaderboards\",\"url\":\"https://www.swebench.com/\"},{\"title\":\"AI Model Benchmarks May 2026 | Compare GPT-5, Claude 4.5, Gemini 2.5, Grok 4 | LM Council\",\"url\":\"https://lmcouncil.ai/benchmarks\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the Aider Polyglot benchmark leaderboard in 2026:\n\n## Aider Polyglot Benchmark Results (2026)\n\nOn multi-language editing (Aider Polyglot), Claude Opus 4.5 leads at 89.4% (Anthropic-reported), with GPT-5 (high) at 88.0%.\n\nClaude Opus 4.6 leads the Aider Polyglot benchmark, consistent with its strong showing on SWE-Bench Verified.\n\nRegarding DeepSeek and Claude Sonnet on this benchmark:\n\n- DeepSeek V3.2-Exp delivers 74.2% on Aider Polyglot at $1.30/run — 22x cheaper than GPT-5.\n- Aider Polyglot has it at 56.9% for DeepSeek R1.\n\nFor Claude Sonnet specifically, while it doesn't appear to be listed on the Aider Polyglot leaderboard in these results, Claude Sonnet 4.6 punches above its weight at 79.6% — still only 1.2 points behind Opus 4.6 and 5x cheaper. on other benchmarks.\n\nAider's polyglot benchmark tests LLMs on 225 challenging Exercism coding exercises across C++, Go, Java, JavaScript, Python, and Rust.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"915548db-4a97-489f-a8bf-2e5f1e29ad9c","timestamp":"2026-05-10T00:10:17.427Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c5ff5ad0-1ecc-4a31-842c-27eef1fffa66","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f740f35c-1312-45f4-81ae-4fc3a513ad86","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6e1f01cb-4356-4ba8-94e6-90a7c6c916fa","agentId":"a7f6f2df056acf347","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GdK5pXNsvtKqr3Xg1VuD5w","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Claude Sonnet 4.6 vs DeepSeek V4 comparison coding 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Claude Sonnet 4.6 vs DeepSeek V4 Pro (High): AI Benchmark Comparison 2026 | BenchLM.ai\",\"url\":\"https://benchlm.ai/compare/claude-sonnet-4-6-vs-deepseek-v4-pro-high\"},{\"title\":\"Claude Sonnet 4.6 vs DeepSeek V4 Flash Comparison (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://www.llmreference.com/compare/claude-sonnet-4-6/deepseek-v4-flash\"},{\"title\":\"Claude Sonnet 4.6 vs DeepSeek V4 Pro Comparison (2026) | LLMReference\",\"url\":\"https://www.llmreference.com/compare/claude-sonnet-4-6/deepseek-v4-pro\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek V4 Flash vs Claude Sonnet 4.6: Which Model Is Best for AI Agent Workflows? | MindStudio\",\"url\":\"https://www.mindstudio.ai/blog/deepseek-v4-flash-vs-claude-sonnet-comparison-agents\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek V4 vs Claude Sonnet 4.6 API: Developer Comparison (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://kissapi.ai/blog/deepseek-v4-vs-claude-sonnet-api-2026.html\"},{\"title\":\"Claude Sonnet 4.6 vs DeepSeek-V4-Pro-Max Comparison\",\"url\":\"https://llm-stats.com/models/compare/claude-sonnet-4-6-vs-deepseek-v4-pro-max\"},{\"title\":\"Claude Sonnet 4.6 vs DeepSeek-V4 Flash - Detailed Performance & Feature Comparison\",\"url\":\"https://docsbot.ai/models/compare/claude-sonnet-4-6/deepseek-v4-flash\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek V4 Pro (Reasoning, Max Effort) vs Claude Sonnet 4.6 (Non-reasoning, High Effort): Model Comparison\",\"url\":\"https://artificialanalysis.ai/models/comparisons/deepseek-v4-pro-vs-claude-sonnet-4-6\"},{\"title\":\"Claude Sonnet 4.6 vs DeepSeek V4 Pro (Comparative Analysis) | Galaxy.ai\",\"url\":\"https://blog.galaxy.ai/compare/claude-sonnet-4-6-vs-deepseek-v4-pro\"},{\"title\":\"Claude Sonnet 4.6 vs DeepSeek-V4-Flash-Max Comparison\",\"url\":\"https://llm-stats.com/models/compare/claude-sonnet-4-6-vs-deepseek-v4-flash-max\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's a comprehensive comparison of Claude Sonnet 4.6 vs DeepSeek V4 for coding:\n\n## Coding Performance\n\nDeepSeek V4 Pro (High)'s sharpest advantage is in coding, where it averages 73.8 against 66.4. More specifically, benchmarks show DeepSeek V4 edges out Claude Sonnet on HumanEval (90% vs 88%) and SWE-bench (80%+ vs ~75%).\n\nHowever, in practice, the difference is more nuanced than those numbers suggest. V4 is genuinely strong at competitive programming-style tasks, handling dynamic programming, graph algorithms, and complex data structures with confidence. Meanwhile, Claude is still the king of doing exactly what you ask.\n\n## Context Window & Capabilities\n\nA major differentiator is context size: DeepSeek V4 Pro (High) gives you the larger context window at 1M, compared with 200K for Claude Sonnet 4.6. DeepSeek's 1M token context window is a game-changer for large codebase understanding—you can feed it an entire repository and ask questions about cross-file dependencies, while Claude's 200K limit means you have to be more selective.\n\n## Pricing\n\nThere's a substantial cost difference. Claude Sonnet 4.6 is $3.00 input / $15.00 output per 1M tokens, versus $1.74 input / $3.48 output per 1M tokens for DeepSeek V4 Pro (High)—roughly 4.3x on output cost alone.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nClaude Sonnet 4.6's consistency, instruction following, and code quality still make it the better choice for interactive development and precision tasks. Choose Claude Sonnet 4.6 when coding workflow support and broader provider choice are central to the workload.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"f364d437-fb0a-4435-be48-8a3b8381da36","timestamp":"2026-05-10T00:10:18.714Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f740f35c-1