{"parentUuid":"49d75b34-65aa-4848-bffd-88af7a38287d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6e1f01cb-4356-4ba8-94e6-90a7c6c916fa","agentId":"a7f6f2df056acf347","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012mbiiAz5VYKoShL4GqPCdY","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"DeepSeek V4 Flash API pricing per million tokens 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"DeepSeek V4 Flash - API Pricing & Benchmarks | OpenRouter\",\"url\":\"https://openrouter.ai/deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash\"},{\"title\":\"Models & Pricing | DeepSeek API Docs\",\"url\":\"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek Pricing 2026: API Cost, Free Tier & Plans Guide\",\"url\":\"https://felloai.com/deepseek-pricing/\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek V4 Pricing & API Migration (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://www.verdent.ai/guides/deepseek-v4-pricing-api-migration-2026\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek V4 Pro API Pricing 2026: Official V4 Prices per 1M Tokens\",\"url\":\"https://devtk.ai/en/models/deepseek-v4/\"},{\"title\":\"Evomap\",\"url\":\"https://evomap.ai/blog/deepseek-v4-api-cheap-tokens-hidden-costs\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek API Pricing: V4 Flash, V4 Pro, Cache Hit, Cache Miss & Output Costs\",\"url\":\"https://chat-deep.ai/pricing/\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek API Pricing 2026: Complete Cost Guide (V4, R1 & Chat) | NxCode\",\"url\":\"https://www.nxcode.io/resources/news/deepseek-api-pricing-complete-guide-2026\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek V4 Pro - API Pricing & Benchmarks | OpenRouter\",\"url\":\"https://openrouter.ai/deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek V4 API Review 2026: Flash vs Pro Guide\",\"url\":\"https://evolink.ai/blog/deepseek-v4-api-review-2026-flash-vs-pro-guide\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here is the current pricing for DeepSeek V4 Flash API in 2026:\n\n## DeepSeek V4 Flash API Pricing per Million Tokens\n\nDeepSeek V4 Flash costs $0.14 per million input tokens and $0.28 per million output tokens.\n\n### Additional Pricing Details:\n\n**Cache-Hit Input:** On V4 Flash, cached input is $0.0028/M — that's a 98% discount versus cache-miss.\n\n**Context & Output:** V4 Flash has a 1,048,576 token context window with a maximum output of 384,000 tokens.\n\n### Key Context:\nA price adjustment took effect from 2026/4/26 12:15 UTC, which reduced cache-hit pricing. DeepSeek V4 launched in preview on April 24, 2026 and ships with a native 1 million token context window at no extra charge.\n\nThese are the standard rates with no promotional discount—V4 Flash is DeepSeek's most cost-efficient model in their V4 lineup.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a3ed8e0a-69fa-4809-a8a6-d039f019431a","timestamp":"2026-05-10T00:10:28.327Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"49d75b34-65aa-4848-bffd-88af7a38287d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"014d8c54-af16-4fb6-baa6-4a3f574b3897","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6e1f01cb-4356-4ba8-94e6-90a7c6c916fa","agentId":"a7f6f2df056acf347","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HJoCht5n4TWDZ8ZGpkaQdn","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Anthropic API DeepSeek API separate billing quota independent accounts\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Anthropic API | DeepSeek API Docs\",\"url\":\"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/anthropic_api\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek API Rate Limits: How They Actually Work (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://deepseekai.guide/api/deepseek-api-rate-limits/\"},{\"title\":\"Models & Pricing | DeepSeek API Docs\",\"url\":\"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing\"},{\"title\":\"Your First API Call | DeepSeek API Docs\",\"url\":\"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek Account Setup: Step-by-Step Guide (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://deepseekai.guide/guides/deepseek-account-setup/\"},{\"title\":\"How to Use DeepSeek-V3.1 API — a practical developer tutorial | by CometAPI | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@mkteam/how-to-use-deepseek-v3-1-api-a-practical-developer-tutorial-d68f491ee2cf\"},{\"title\":\"When you consolidate 15+ separate AI subscriptions into one plan, what actually improves beyond the invoice? - Enterprise Adoption & Procurement - Latenode Official Community\",\"url\":\"https://community.latenode.com/t/when-you-consolidate-15-separate-ai-subscriptions-into-one-plan-what-actually-improves-beyond-the-invoice/57231\"},{\"title\":\"How do you actually quantify the cost savings when you're not paying for five separate ai model subscriptions anymore? - Enterprise Adoption & Procurement - Latenode Official Community\",\"url\":\"https://community.latenode.com/t/how-do-you-actually-quantify-the-cost-savings-when-youre-not-paying-for-five-separate-ai-model-subscriptions-anymore/56414\"},{\"title\":\"\\\"Anthropic Billing Guide: Manage Your Claude API Costs Effectively\\\" - Crazyrouter\",\"url\":\"https://crazyrouter.com/en/blog/anthropic-billing-guide-claude-api-costs\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek API Pricing 2026: Complete Cost Guide (V4, R1 & Chat) | NxCode\",\"url\":\"https://www.nxcode.io/resources/news/deepseek-api-pricing-complete-guide-2026\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding Anthropic API, DeepSeek API, separate billing, quotas, and independent accounts:\n\n## Separate APIs and Billing\n\nAnthropic and DeepSeek maintain separate API services, each with its own API key and billing cycle with independent quota management. They are distinct services operated by different companies with their own billing infrastructure.\n\n## DeepSeek's Anthropic API Compatibility\n\nDeepSeek's API has added support for the Anthropic API format, with the base_url being https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic. With simple configuration, you can integrate the capabilities of DeepSeek into the Anthropic API ecosystem. This means you can use the Anthropic SDK to call DeepSeek models by changing the base URL and API key.\n\nHowever, DeepSeek publishes an Anthropic-compatible surface against the same base URL, so the Anthropic SDK works by swapping base_url and api_key, and the rate-limit behaviour is identical to the native OpenAI-compatible endpoint.\n\n## Rate Limits and Quotas\n\nImportantly, DeepSeek does not currently support raising the dynamic rate limit on individual accounts, and there is a unified pricing standard with no tiered plans. The API dynamically limits user concurrency based on server load and returns an HTTP 429 the moment you reach that limit.\n\nIn summary: Anthropic and DeepSeek maintain completely independent billing and account systems, even though DeepSeek offers compatibility with the Anthropic API format for integration purposes.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6469eec6-29c8-4b66-8466-cad33de2a529","timestamp":"2026-05-10T00:10:29.031Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"014d8c54-af16-4fb6-baa6-4a3f574b3897","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6469eec6-29c8-4b66-8466-cad33de2a529","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a7f6f2df056acf347","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01CzQ3y4q52ofteHQfAoAtAM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"数据齐了，输出结论。\n\n---\n\n## 性能对比 (代码生成主要)\n\n| Benchmark | Sonnet 4.6 | DeepSeek V4-Flash | DeepSeek V4-Pro |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| SWE-bench Verified | 79.6% | 79.0% | 80.6% (Pro-Max) |\n| HumanEval | 92.1% | ~88% | ~90% |\n| LiveCodeBench | 72.4% | 91.6% | 93.5% |\n| Aider Polyglot | ~79% (Sonnet 同档) | (无独立数) | V3.2-Exp 74.2%,V4 未公布 |\n| 数学/推理 (MATH) | 89% | 中档 | 73.8 综合 (Pro-High 编码均分) |\n\n**结论**：三家在 SWE-bench 上 ±1 分钟级（79-80.6%），差距小到可忽略；DeepSeek V4 在**竞赛式 LiveCodeBench 显著领先**（+19-21 pt，胜在算法/DP/图题快速生成），Sonnet 在**指令跟随 + 代码质量稳定性 + 规范遵循**上更强（\"king of doing exactly what you ask\"）。我们 PoC 是\"生成 Python cut/hint 代码 + 跟项目约束（exactness contract、AI safety contract）\",**指令遵守权重远高于算法 brilliance** —— Sonnet 优势更对题。\n\n## 额度独立性\n\n- **Anthropic 跟 DeepSeek 完全独立**：不同公司、不同账号、不同 billing、不同 rate limit。Anthropic key 跑 OpenEvolve 不消耗任何 DeepSeek quota，反之亦然。（DeepSeek 有 Anthropic-compatible endpoint `api.deepseek.com/anthropic`，仅 SDK 兼容层，账户依旧独立。）\n- **定价 (per 1M tokens)**：\n  - Sonnet 4.6: $3 in / $15 out\n  - V4-Flash: $0.14 in / $0.28 out（约 21x 便宜，cache-hit 再 98% 折扣到 $0.0028）\n  - V4-Pro: $1.74 in / $3.48 out\n- **500 次 PoC 成本估算**（假设单次 ~5K in / 2K out tokens）：Sonnet ≈ $22；V4-Flash ≈ $0.6；V4-Pro ≈ $7。Sonnet 绝对值 $20 量级，对个人 budget 仍 negligible。\n\n## 推荐\n\n**主 backend: Sonnet 4.6 单跑，不混搭。**\n\n理由：\n1. PoC 是 \"代码生成 + 严格遵守 AI safety contract（不能写 checkpoints / 不能改 proof 源）\"，**指令遵循 > 算法暴力**，Sonnet 更对题；DeepSeek 的 LiveCodeBench 优势在 cut evolution 这类\"评测器打分\"场景里大概率被指令漂移吃掉。\n2. 额度完全独立，跟你日常 Claude Code session 不抢；500 次 ~$22 完全可接受。\n3. 单 backend 省掉 router + prompt 适配 + 双 SDK 维护成本，PoC 阶段不值得搞混搭。混搭是后续真量产（5000+ iter 量级）才考虑的事。\n\n驳原 audit \"V4-Flash 主 + Sonnet 副\"：成本节约 $20 vs 两套 SDK + 评分对齐 + 失败模式调试，ROI 是负的。\n\nSources:\n- [Claude Sonnet 4.6 Complete Guide / NxCode](https://www.nxcode.io/resources/news/claude-sonnet-4-6-complete-guide-benchmarks-pricing-2026)\n- [DeepSeek V4 Complete Guide / Codersera](https://codersera.com/blog/deepseek-v4-complete-guide-2026/)\n- [Sonnet 4.6 vs V4 Pro / BenchLM](https://benchlm.ai/compare/claude-sonnet-4-6-vs-deepseek-v4-pro-high)\n- [Sonnet 4.6 vs V4 Flash / LLMReference](https://www.llmreference.com/compare/claude-sonnet-4-6/deepseek-v4-flash)\n- [DeepSeek API Anthropic Compat / DeepSeek Docs](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/anthropic_api)\n- [DeepSeek V4 API Pricing / DeepSeek Docs](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing)\n- [Aider Leaderboards](https://aider.chat/docs/leaderboards/)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1112,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1767,"cache_read_input_tokens":32621,"output_tokens":1653,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1767},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1112,"output_tokens":1653,"cache_read_input_tokens":32621,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1767,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1767,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CasvCgEbqAbg2Wgv2k47f","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"cf73a74a-fdda-4159-8f78-3ba8394aab8f","timestamp":"2026-05-10T00:10:58.861Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
